BT /F2 17 Tf 54 730.0 Td (Cyber Risk Assessment & Risk Management Policy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703.0 Td (Hewlett Packard Enterprise \(HPE\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 689.0 Td (Document Owner: Global Chief Information Security Officer \(CISO\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 675.0 Td (Classification: HPE Internal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 661.0 Td (Version: 4.2 | Effective Date: 2026-01-15 | Next Review: 2027-01-15) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 641.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 615.0 Td (1. Purpose) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 592.0 Td (This policy establishes the enterprise-wide methodology by which Hewlett Packard Enterprise) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 578.0 Td (identifies, analyzes, evaluates, and treats cyber risk across its global operations. It ensures that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 564.0 Td (risk-based decisions protecting HPE GreenLake edge-to-cloud services, Aruba networking, ProLiant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 550.0 Td (compute infrastructure, and the SAP S/4HANA ERP environment are consistent, defensible, and aligned) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 536.0 Td (with the corporate risk appetite approved by the Board Audit Committee.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 510.0 Td (2. Scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 487.0 Td (This policy applies to all HPE business units, subsidiaries, and third-party service providers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 473.0 Td (worldwide. The assessment scope encompasses all information assets, production and non-production) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 459.0 Td (systems, cloud tenancies, and OT/IoT boundaries that store, process, or transmit HPE or customer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 445.0 Td (data. Explicit scope boundaries are documented for each assessment engagement, including the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 431.0 Td (GreenLake control plane, Aruba Central management infrastructure, ProLiant firmware supply chain,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 417.0 Td (and the SAP S/4HANA financial and manufacturing modules. Assets are enumerated from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 403.0 Td (authoritative Configuration Management Database \(CMDB\) prior to each cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 377.0 Td (3. Risk Assessment Methodology) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 354.0 Td (HPE applies a structured risk framework aligned to NIST SP 800-30, NIST CSF 2.0, and ISO/IEC 27005.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 340.0 Td (The assessment process follows five phases: \(1\) asset and system characterization, \(2\) threat and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 326.0 Td (vulnerability identification, \(3\) inherent risk analysis, \(4\) control evaluation and residual risk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 312.0 Td (determination, and \(5\) risk treatment and reporting.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 54 288.0 Td (3.1 Risk Scoring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 266.5 Td (Each identified risk is scored on two dimensions:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 246.5 Td (- Likelihood / Probability - the assessed probability that a given threat will successfully) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 232.5 Td (  exploit a vulnerability, rated on a 1-5 scale informed by current threat intelligence,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 218.5 Td (  historical incident data, and control maturity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 204.5 Td (- Impact / Consequence - the severity and magnitude of harm to HPE should the risk materialize,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 190.5 Td (  evaluated across financial, operational, regulatory, safety, and brand-reputation consequence) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 176.5 Td (  categories, also rated 1-5.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 156.5 Td (The product of likelihood and impact yields the inherent \(gross\) risk rating - the exposure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 142.5 Td (calculated *before* the application of mitigating controls. After accounting for the design and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 128.5 Td (operating effectiveness of existing controls, a residual \(net\) risk rating is derived, representing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 114.5 Td (the remaining exposure retained by HPE.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 88.5 Td (4. Assessment Cadence) Tj ET
endstream
