BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738.0 Td (Risk assessments are conducted on a defined schedule to maintain currency:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 718.0 Td (- Annual enterprise-wide risk assessment covering all in-scope business units and crown-jewel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 704.0 Td (  systems.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690.0 Td (- Quarterly assessments for high-criticality environments, including the GreenLake control plane) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 676.0 Td (  and SAP S/4HANA.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 662.0 Td (- Event-driven / periodic assessments triggered by material change - new product launches,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 648.0 Td (  mergers and acquisitions, significant architecture changes, or emerging zero-day threats.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 622.0 Td (5. Threat Intelligence Integration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 599.0 Td (Risk analysis is enriched by HPE's Cyber Threat Intelligence \(CTI\) function, which continuously) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 585.0 Td (profiles relevant adversary groups, attack campaigns, and tactics, techniques, and procedures \(TTPs\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 571.0 Td (mapped to the MITRE ATT&CK framework. Intelligence is aggregated from multiple sources and feeds,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 557.0 Td (including CISA advisories and Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog, sector ISAC memberships) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 543.0 Td (\(IT-ISAC\), commercial vendor intel subscriptions, open-source feeds, and internal telemetry from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 529.0 Td (Aruba and GreenLake sensors. This threat intelligence directly informs likelihood scoring and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 515.0 Td (ensures that assessments reflect the active adversary landscape targeting the technology sector.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 489.0 Td (6. Risk Register) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 466.0 Td (All identified risks are recorded in the enterprise Risk Register, the authoritative inventory and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 452.0 Td (catalog of cyber risk maintained within the HPE GRC platform. Each register entry captures the asset) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 438.0 Td (affected, threat scenario, inherent and residual scores, assigned controls, treatment decision,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 424.0 Td (target remediation date, and status. The Risk Register is reviewed monthly by the Cyber Risk Council) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 410.0 Td (and reported quarterly to executive leadership.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 384.0 Td (7. Risk Appetite and Tolerance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 361.0 Td (The Board-approved risk appetite defines the level of cyber risk HPE is willing to accept in pursuit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 347.0 Td (of its business objectives. Quantitative risk tolerance thresholds are established per risk tier:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 333.0 Td (residual risks scoring within the "Low" band fall inside tolerance and may be formally accepted,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 319.0 Td (while risks exceeding defined thresholds require documented treatment plans and executive sign-off.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 305.0 Td (Any acceptance of risk above tolerance requires explicit approval from the CISO and the relevant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 291.0 Td (Business Unit executive.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 265.0 Td (8. Risk Ownership and Accountability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 242.0 Td (Every risk in the register is assigned a named Risk Owner - the accountable business or technical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 228.0 Td (leader responsible for the affected asset and for driving the treatment decision to completion. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 214.0 Td (CISO organization provides oversight, facilitation, and challenge, but accountability for accepting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 200.0 Td (or remediating a risk rests with the designated responsible party. Ownership assignments are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 186.0 Td (validated during each assessment cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 160.0 Td (9. Risk Treatment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 137.0 Td (For each risk exceeding tolerance, the Risk Owner, supported by the security team, selects one or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 123.0 Td (more treatment strategies:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 103.0 Td (- Mitigate / Remediate - implement or strengthen technical and administrative controls to reduce) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 89.0 Td (  likelihood or impact \(the default and preferred response\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 75.0 Td (- Transfer - shift financial exposure through cyber insurance or contractual indemnification) Tj ET
endstream
